  The reel_script says the farmers 'warned' (எச்சரித்தார்) while the article says Venugopal spoke of the plan; minor, but the slides call it a 'எச்சரிக்கை' which is consistent. Not a fact error by itself.
  The slide 'ஏன் எதிர்ப்பு?' says farmers' fear is 'அச்சம்', consistent with article; however the slide 'போராட்டம்' states the rally was held in front of the tahsildar office, which the article supports.
  The reel_script states 'கருப்பு கொடி கட்டப்படும்' for all villages from Sunday; the article says 'ஞாயிறு (இன்று) முதல்' meaning from today (Sunday), so the reel's phrasing is acceptable, but it omits that the article's date reference is 'இன்று' and the event of the protest was 'நேற்று' - the reel does not state the protest happened yesterday, which is a missing timing fact.
  The caption's English line 'Mettupalayam farmers oppose elephant camp, black flag protest' contains 'black flag protest' which is not wording from the article; the caption also calls the protest a 'கருப்பு கொடி' campaign, which is a slight overstatement.
